course: dictionary
lesson: 9154
title: Snore and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and it can be a different kind of word. «Snore» is a verb when you do it («Dad snores») and a noun when it is the sound itself («a loud snore»). It means to breathe noisily while asleep, with a rough sound in the nose or throat.
explain: Use the sentence to choose the right meaning. «Hedgehogs snore, snuffle and grunt, and they got their name because they root about in hedges.» Snuffle and grunt are animal sounds too, so snore here is the noisy breathing of a sleeping animal. Swap in your meaning and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Snore has an informal meaning too. «A snore» or «snore-fest» means something very boring. A sleepy film is not a noisy breath, so ask what the sentence is about before you choose a meaning.
fact: «Snore» means to breathe noisily while asleep, with a rough sound in the nose or throat.
fact: «A snore» is the noun for the sound of snoring.
fact: Snoring happens when air shakes the soft parts in the throat.
fact: «Snore» is also informal slang for something very boring, as in «snore-fest».
fact: In stories, snores often show a character is fast asleep, which is why writers use «Zzz».
exercise: In «Dad snores and keeps everyone awake», what kind of word is snores? | a noun (a thing) | *a verb (an action) | a question word | an adjective (a describing word)
exercise: «The film was a real snore, and half the class fell asleep.» What does snore mean here? | *Something very boring | A fast race | A loud snoring sound | A type of bird
exercise: «Bulldogs ... very flat-faced dogs often struggle to breathe, snore and overheat easily.» What does snore mean in this sentence? | Bark at strangers | Run very fast | Eat too much food | *Breathe noisily while asleep
test: The poem says: «he snores at my feet all night». Snore here means | to eat quietly at night | *breathe noisily while asleep | to bark loudly at the moon | to walk away from someone
test: «A snore» is a noun. Which sentence uses it correctly? | She snored a delicious cake. | Snore the blue table now. | The snore ran across the field. | *The loud snore woke the whole camp.
exam: Read: «A sleeping person breathes, snores and has a beating heart.» Which statement is true? | Snoring means running very fast. | People never make any sound while asleep. | *People breathe and snore while they are asleep. | A beating heart stops when you sleep.
